    "intro_html":  "Pepper steak is the takeout order that never disappoints and never quite justifies its price. Sliced steak, green and red peppers, onion, and a glossy soy and ginger sauce over rice. Made at home it takes about half an hour once the slicing is done, and every single ingredient in it is something you can buy at a normal grocery store. Each bowl runs {{cal}} calories and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
